      "comment": "Quintilian’s word, made as a translation of Greek προσῳδία (<span lang=\"la\">ad</span> + <span lang=\"la\">cantus</span>): the accent that falls on one syllable of a word. In late Latin it is also a blast of trumpets (Amm.). The beat of a verse is <span lang=\"la\">ictus</span>, which is not the same thing as the word’s accent."
